  "help": {
    "format": "markdown",
    "content": "\nEPA-ng places aligned query sequences onto a fixed reference phylogeny using maximum likelihood. All query and reference sequences must have the same alignment columns. Reference tree tips must match the reference alignment identifiers.\n\nThe output is a jplace JSON document containing candidate placement edges, likelihood weights and branch lengths. It can be used by GAPPA to graft query sequences, assign taxonomy, or visualize placement mass. The tool retains multiple placements by default (minimum weight 0.01, maximum seven) so uncertainty remains available downstream. A maximum of one retains only the best placement.\n\nThe model input accepts a RAxML-NG model description, including fixed parameters in braces (for example, `GTR+G{0.5}`). This tool does not estimate a reference tree or align sequences.\n    "
  }
}